  "grammar_explanations": [
    {
      "slug": "comparative: -er than",
      "title_form": "Comparativos con -er than",
      "title_target": "Comparatives with -er than",
      "description_md_form": "Para comparar dos cosas en inglés, usamos **adjetivos cortos** (de una o dos sílabas) con la terminación **-er** y la palabra **than** (que).\n\n**Estructura:** `[cosa 1] + [verbo] + [adjetivo + -er] + than + [cosa 2]`\n\n**Ejemplos:**\n- *This chair is **lower** than that one.* (Esta silla es más baja que esa.)\n- *The new blanket is **softer** than the old one.* (La manta nueva es más suave que la vieja.)\n\n**Reglas ortográficas:**\n- Adjetivo + **-er**: `low` → `lower`, `soft` → `softer`.\n- Termina en **-e**: solo añade **-r**: `wide` → `wider`.\n- Termina en **consonante + y**: cambia **y** por **i** y añade **-er**: `heavy` → `heavier`.\n\n**Importante:** `than` siempre acompaña al comparativo. No lo olvides.",
      "description_md_target": "To compare two things in English, we use **short adjectives** (one or two syllables) with the ending **-er** and the word **than**.\n\n**Structure:** `[thing 1] + [verb] + [adjective + -er] + than + [thing 2]`\n\n**Examples:**\n- *This chair is **lower** than that one.*\n- *The new blanket is **softer** than the old one.*\n\n**Spelling rules:**\n- Adjective + **-er**: `low` → `lower`, `soft` → `softer`.\n- Ends in **-e**: just add **-r**: `wide` → `wider`.\n- Ends in **consonant + y**: change **y** to **i** and add **-er**: `heavy` → `heavier`.\n\n**Important:** `than` always goes with the comparative. Do not forget it.",
      "grammar_structure": "Subject + to be + adjective(-er) + than + object",
      "conjugation_table": {
        "name": "comparative_adjectives",
        "headers": [
          "Adjetivo",
          "Comparativo",
          "Regla"
        ],
        "rows": [
          [
            "low",
            "lower",
            "adjetivo + -er"
          ],
          [
            "soft",
            "softer",
            "adjetivo + -er"
          ],
          [
            "wide",
            "wider",
            "termina en -e: + -r"
          ],
          [
            "heavy",
            "heavier",
            "consonante + y: y → i + -er"
          ]
        ]
      },
